From: guille-vega <guillermo.vega@balena.io>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 07:45:38 +0100
Subject: imx8m: Pad the DDR firmware data memory to 2 KiB

Without binman the SPL finds the DDR training firmware after its own
image and DTB with a fixed layout: the instruction memory padded to 32
KiB and the data memory to 16 KiB, for the 1D and the 2D firmware, and
the FIT hash after them. The data memory blobs are below 2 KiB, so most
of these 96 KiB are padding, and with a SPL as large as the one with HAB
they reach the early malloc pool, gd and the stack at the top of the SPL
OCRAM area.

Pad the data memory to 2 KiB, which saves 28 KiB. imx-mkimage has to
pad the firmware the same way.

Signed-off-by: guille-vega <guillermo.vega@balena.io>
---
 arch/arm/mach-imx/spl.c      | 4 ++--
 drivers/ddr/imx/phy/helper.c | 4 ++--
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-imx/spl.c b/arch/arm/mach-imx/spl.c
index 2ca3d2b..9e9325a 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-imx/spl.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-imx/spl.c
@@ -365,10 +365,10 @@ static int spl_verify_fit_hash(const void *fit)
 #if CONFIG_IS_ENABLED(OF_CONTROL)
 	if (gd->fdt_blob && !fdt_check_header(gd->fdt_blob)) {
 		fit_hash = roundup((unsigned long)&_end +
-				     fdt_totalsize(gd->fdt_blob), 4) + 0x18000;
+				     fdt_totalsize(gd->fdt_blob), 4) + 0x11000;
 	}
 #else
-	fit_hash = (unsigned long)&_end + 0x18000;
+	fit_hash = (unsigned long)&_end + 0x11000;
 #endif
 
 	size = fdt_totalsize(fit);
diff --git a/drivers/ddr/imx/phy/helper.c b/drivers/ddr/imx/phy/helper.c
index 7577a03..ef42d65 100644
--- a/drivers/ddr/imx/phy/helper.c
+++ b/drivers/ddr/imx/phy/helper.c
@@ -18,8 +18,8 @@
 DECLARE_GLOBAL_DATA_PTR;
 
 #define IMEM_LEN 32768 /* byte */
-#define DMEM_LEN 16384 /* byte */
-#define IMEM_2D_OFFSET	49152
+#define DMEM_LEN 2048 /* byte */
+#define IMEM_2D_OFFSET	34816
 
 #define IMEM_OFFSET_ADDR 0x00050000
 #define DMEM_OFFSET_ADDR 0x00054000
